    {
      "sentences": [
        "TEB36",
        "TF161"
      ],
      "description": "An earlier survey can leave a permanently dredged slope. If its final profile is linear from 200 m to 93 m, the crossing takes 26.8596 min rather than the claimed invariant 29.1883 min. Ending the survey does not restore the seabed."
    },
    {
      "sentences": [
        "T8491",
        "T1E46"
      ],
      "description": "Deepening only a short region near the landward endpoint by 33 m produces a time arbitrarily close to 29.1883 min as that region shrinks. A new linear profile from 200 m to 93 m instead gives 26.8596 min. The endpoint increment alone does not determine the integral."
    },
    {
      "sentences": [
        "TA114",
        "T5E18"
      ],
      "description": "At the authors' outside-regime example wavelength of 2 km, their reference speed sqrt(g*lambda/(2*pi)) is approximately 55.9 m/s. Finite-depth gravity-wave phase speed cannot exceed sqrt(g*h), which is at most 44.3 m/s anywhere on this shelf. The deep-water reference expression therefore cannot describe that example."
